# The pinned Debian base. One file, so the image build and the authoritative test tier
# cannot drift apart. Shell-sourceable, and parsed as `KEY=VALUE` lines by everything else.
#
# Changing either line changes every resolved package version, which changes the ISO hash.
# It is a release-affecting edit: bump it deliberately, regenerate build/apt-versions.txt
# in the same commit, and expect the reproducibility guard to notice.
#
# `snapshot.debian.org` serves the archive as it stood at this instant, forever, which is
# what lets a stranger rebuild a release after the live mirror has moved on. It also means
# `Valid-Until` in the Release file is long past — the apt config must carry
# `[check-valid-until=no]`, and that is a consequence of pinning, not a weakening of it.

DEBIAN_SUITE=trixie
DEBIAN_SNAPSHOT=20260901T000000Z
DEBIAN_ARCH=amd64
